-- `/std/Flt/Env/bind`'s record holds `/std/State/bind(m.0, (a) => f(a).0)`, whose field lambda runs the lambda it is handed, which applies `f`. The summary of how `bind` applies its parameters hands the lambda what `/std/State/bind`'s leading lambdas apply of it, nothing, so its body is never walked, and the part `bind` holds grades no argument that is no parameter: `bind` states `f` applied nowhere, `/spin`'s callback is handed where nothing applies it, and running `/spin(0)` runs `/spin(0)` again. The proof `Box` holds is read off a run that never ends.
use /std/{Nat};
use /std/Flt/{Env};
use /std/Bool/{False};

struct Box: Type {
    p: False,
}

let spin(n: Nat) -> Env(Box) =
    Env/bind(Env/pure(n), (x) => spin(x));

Env/run(spin(0)).0.p
